  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "Address the bug in skip location reporting when tests are skipped using @pytest.mark.skip or skipif. When running tests with 'pytest -rs', the expected behavior is that the skip location points to the test item itself (for example, 'test_it.py:3: unconditional skip'). However, when the '--runxfail' option is added, the location is incorrectly reported as coming from 'src/_pytest/skipping.py' (for example, 'src/_pytest/skipping.py:238: unconditional skip'). The bug is located in the pytest_runtest_makereport hook within src/_pytest/skipping.py. This feature requires fixing the logic so that '--runxfail' does not interfere with the proper skip location reporting.",
    "hint_texts": "Modify the conditional logic in the pytest_runtest_makereport function found in src/_pytest/skipping.py. Change the current 'elif' statement to an 'if' to ensure that the skip location is correctly derived from the test item's stored data. Ensure that the fix isolates the influence of the '--runxfail' flag only to xfail handling and does not affect skip marker processing.",
    "entrypoint": "src/_pytest/skipping.py \u2013 specifically within the pytest_runtest_makereport hook where the condition checking for a skipped test is made (around the modified condition from 'elif' to 'if').",
